ifa/issues/025 -- branch-correlation narrowing is not implemented: `a` is provably Dog in one arm and Cat in the other (the second `if flag:` correlates with the first), but only isinstance / is-None are recognised as discriminators. Since ifa/158 made every violation fatal, the two "illegal call argument type" violations REFUSE this valid program (it used to warn and then run correctly). The .check records no diagnostics, so this flips to PASS when correlation lands (tail duplication at the second test) or when a union member lacking the method becomes a permissive runtime check.
